        "id": "human-a11y-review",
        "statement": "A human completed an end-to-end accessibility review of this component.",
        "verification": "manual",
        "note": "2026-10-30 (Claude, Storybook 6010, Chromium; real key presses): label is a <label for> the control and carries ${id}-label for aria-labelledby controls (Combobox, MultiCombobox); fieldDescribedBy lists the status message then the helper (verified on Company size: named by its label, described by 'Choose a company size', aria-invalid only for error). Actions: native buttons named by aria-label; DS Tooltip opens on keyboard focus (Shift+Tab onto Paste shows 'Paste'), not pointer-only. Menu action: Enter opens, ArrowDown moves Use-the-size-from-last-time -> Reset, Escape closes and returns focus to the trigger; aria-haspopup=menu, aria-expanded tracks state. Focus ring sits inside the 32px box, 4px clear of the control (measured). Hit area 44px on coarse pointers. No motion of its own; Menu and Tooltip carry the DS reduced-motion handling. Forced colors: icon ButtonText, ring Highlight 3px inset. The label is always required; hideLabel hides it visually and keeps it as the accessible name.",
        "reviewedAt": "2026-10-30"
      }
